1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,280
 This is going to be a quick lecture to understand what is the need for retrieval, augmented

2
00:00:05,280 --> 00:00:08,740
 generation or RAG.

3
00:00:08,740 --> 00:00:14,120
 So if you see the biggest challenge with the foundation model is lack of proprietary information

4
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:16,680
 or enterprise information.

5
00:00:16,680 --> 00:00:21,080
 So we know that the foundation models are trained on generic internet data.

6
00:00:21,080 --> 00:00:27,320
 So if you ask it a question that is highly customized to your organization or enterprise,

7
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:29,760
 it will not be able to answer.

8
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:36,200
 Second, so it does not have an up-to-date information post-training cut-off date.

9
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:40,280
 So if you see any base foundation model that is available on Amazon Betterock, it will

10
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:42,280
 have a training cut-off date.

11
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:46,560
 So maybe it has a training cut-off date of December 2024.

12
00:00:46,560 --> 00:00:51,280
 So any information post that it will not be aware of.

13
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:56,120
 So those are the challenges that RAG-based system tries to overcome.

14
00:00:56,120 --> 00:01:02,340
 So retrieval, augmented generation or RAG, equip foundation models with proprietary information

15
00:01:02,340 --> 00:01:06,400
 by fetching the data from the company data sources.

16
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:11,840
 So it can also overcome the challenges of no up-to-date information post-training cut-off

17
00:01:11,840 --> 00:01:18,280
 date through external sources such as documents and so on.

18
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:22,360
 Now let us going to understand this through an example.

19
00:01:22,360 --> 00:01:28,080
 So let us say we are trying to build an e-learning chatbot which helps employees learn AI

20
00:01:28,080 --> 00:01:29,080
 technologies.

21
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:33,720
 Now let us say we have built a generative AI application only using the foundation model.

22
00:01:33,720 --> 00:01:40,480
 And employee now asks a question to the foundation model which says what is the RAG reference

23
00:01:40,480 --> 00:01:44,560
 architecture in my XYZ organization?

24
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:48,960
 Now let us say this question goes to our generative AI application built on top of Amazon

25
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:53,760
 in bedrock so Amazon bedrock is going to route this question to one of the foundation models

26
00:01:53,760 --> 00:02:00,360
 maybe let us say entroping in this case and entropic is going to return with the response.

27
00:02:00,360 --> 00:02:05,960
 Unfortunately I do not have enough contextual information to answer this question because

28
00:02:05,960 --> 00:02:10,200
 I do not know what is the RAG reference architecture for XYZ organization.

29
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:15,600
 So it is going to come back with a generic answer or it is going to say it does not have

30
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:17,600
 enough contextual information.

31
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:21,120
 So that is where RAG comes into play.

32
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:25,560
 Let us assume your data is in the share point where you have PDF documents related to

33
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:29,360
 Amazon bedrock EC2 and some of the other services.

34
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:34,760
 Now let us also assume you have organization Gen AI reference architecture repository where

35
00:02:34,760 --> 00:02:39,600
 you store the reference architecture for all the architecture patterns.

36
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:44,840
 So now what we can do is the Gen AI application built on top of Amazon bedrock can integrate

37
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:49,920
 with these knowledge sources within the organization then you can use the intelligence

38
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:57,160
 of the foundation model but also integrate it with the enterprise data source to get

39
00:02:57,160 --> 00:03:03,800
 the contextual information and it also solve the second problem of the cut off date because

40
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:07,200
 all these documents can have the latest information.

41
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:11,000
 So even if the foundation model does not have the latest information it can retrieve it

42
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:15,440
 from these documents or other external sources.

43
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:17,080
 So now what is the RAG?

44
00:03:17,080 --> 00:03:22,640
 RAG is the process of optimizing the output of a large language model by supplementing

45
00:03:22,640 --> 00:03:29,480
 the knowledge of a large language model with internal organization data source.

46
00:03:29,480 --> 00:03:32,080
 Okay, so that is pretty much it from this lecture.

47
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:33,080
 I will see in the next lecture.

48
00:03:33,080 --> 00:03:33,280
 Thank you.

